t is treated as proof -> fix: independently compile candidate source in the live package, run axiom/trust scans, obtain both reviews, and only then integrate. FF15 remained pending in this rollout. [Task 2]\n637:# Task Group: lean/stabilizer standalone Lean tensor-product and trace formalization\n640:applies_to: cwd=lean/stabilizer (source context=source-workspace); reuse_rule=reuse the checked algebraic modules and analytic-obligation checklist only after rechecking pinned mathlib and source assumptions\n646:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T19-10-40-cRYC-standalone_lean_stabilizer_hyperfinite_formalization_blocked.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T21-10-40-019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T03:04:54+00:00, thread_id=019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2, partial: algebraic results checked; full theorem blocked)\n656:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T19-10-40-cRYC-standalone_lean_stabilizer_hyperfinite_formalization_blocked.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T21-10-40-019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T03:04:54+00:00, thread_id=019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2, blocked: source and library lack required analytic inputs)\n670:- P47, P48, P49, P50, P51, SOT, WOT, bicommutant, Kaplansky density, GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean, aristotle_autopilot.timer, tg-send\n678:- when the user approved unattended automation and Telegram notifications -> halt and alert on blocked/failed/partial/unverified closeouts, but keep routine successful progress quiet [Task 3]\n693:- symptom: strong closedness is treated as density of the original C*-algebra -> fix: distinguish retention of limits in `M` from bounded approximants supplied by Kaplansky density. An attempted P49A/P49B/P49C plan patch failed context matching, so inspect `PLAN.md`, TOML, and `state.json` and make a narrow verified update