{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '637,705p' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md && sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T19-10-40-cRYC-standalone_lean_stabilizer_hyperfinite_formalization_blocked.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Task Group: lean/stabilizer standalone Lean tensor-product and trace formalization\n\nscope: separate, approval-gated Lean audit/formalization of the proposed stabilizer-region tensor-product theorem, with dependency-gated automation and an explicit SOT/WOT-bicommutant-Kaplansky stop boundary\napplies_to: cwd=lean/stabilizer (source context=source-workspace); reuse_rule=reuse the checked algebraic modules and analytic-obligation checklist only after rechecking pinned mathlib and source assumptions\n\n## Task 1: audit the manuscript target and formalize the algebraic layer\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T19-10-40-cRYC-standalone_lean_stabilizer_hyperfinite_formalization_blocked.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T21-10-40-019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T03:04:54+00:00, thread_id=019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2, partial: algebraic results checked; full theorem blocked)\n\n### keywords\n\n- StarAlgEquiv, isUnitalTracial_pullback, CStarEquivExtension.lean, CoherentPhaseQubitState.lean, AlgebraicLimitTraceTransport.lean, UHF, GNS, II_∞, hyperfinite-II1\n\n## Task 2: preserve the full C*- and von Neumann theorem boundary\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T19-10-40-cRYC-standalone_lean_stabilizer_hyperfinite_formalization_blocked.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T21-10-40-019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T03:04:54+00:00, thread_id=019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2, blocked: source and library lack required analytic inputs)\n\n### keywords\n\n- gLU, refinement maps, Pauli multiplier, C*-completion, product-state factorization, quasi-equivalence, bicommutant, normal trace, hyperfinite factor classification, PROGRESS.md\n\n## Task 3: dependency-gate automation and the topology/Kaplansky sublane\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-07T10-48-46-yBcb-stabilizer_formalization_topology_kaplansky_automation.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/07/rollout-2026-08-07T12-48-46-019fdbd6-fa8d-7f73-81c9-8ced776423e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-07T10:50:49+00:00, thread_id=019fdbd6-fa8d-7f73-81c9-8ced776423e7, partial: algebraic transport checked; topology packets and timer require live recheck)\n\n### keywords\n\n- P47, P48, P49, P50, P51, SOT, WOT, bicommutant, Kaplansky density, GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean, aristotle_autopilot.timer, tg-send\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user asked for “a new folder, not in the overleaf repo” and requested an explanation before starting -> preserve the separate project boundary and approval-gated setup [Task 1]\n- when the user said the existing proof may contain errors -> treat manuscript claims as hypotheses to audit, not authoritative facts [Task 1]\n- when the user requested a tracial state induced by the tensor product -> track state existence separately from algebraic isomorphism and factor classification [Task 1]\n- when the user said “we need the theorem… let’s be complete” -> develop the missing topology machinery as a genuine dependency-gated theorem effort; do not package the load-bearing result as an interface/axiom [Task 3]\n- when the user approved unattended automation and Telegram notifications -> halt and alert on blocked/failed/partial/unverified closeouts, but keep routine successful progress quiet [Task 3]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- `B(H) \\bar⊗ R` has a tracial state only for finite-dimensional `H`; for infinite-dimensional `H`, its relevant trace is faithful normal semifinite and the factor is `II_∞`. [Task 1]\n- Checked modules: `Formalization/TraceTransport.lean` proves `StabilizerHyperfinite.isUnitalTracial_pullback`; `CStarEquivExtension.lean` establishes continuity/isometry only for supplied complex C*-algebra `StarAlgEquiv`s; `AlgebraicLimitStarHom.lean`/`AlgebraicLimitTraceTransport.lean` are algebraic direct limits; `CoherentPhaseQubitState.lean` proves the selected-Z phase-weighted expectation from coherent finite-stage data. [Task 1]\n- `lake build`, focused module builds, axiom audits, and two-pass `pdflatex` for `blueprints/001-tensor-product-trace.tex` passed. There were no `sorry`, `admit`, or user axioms in checked sources. [Task 1]\n- Missing inputs remain coherent finite-stage gLU/refinement maps, Pauli multiplier/involution and phase calibration, quasi-local C*-completion, product-state factorization, normal/spatial GNS-bicommutant identification, and hyperfinite-factor classification. [Task 2]\n- `P48` constructs the decreasing projection tower and strong-limit `q`, retaining `q ∈ M` under explicit lattice/support/representation hypotheses via commutant closedness and `M=(M')'`; it does not prove the analytic double-commutant theorem. Pinned Mathlib has WOT primitives and generic strong convergence, but defines concrete `VonNeumannAlgebra` by double commutant and lacks the analytic SOT/WOT equivalence and Kaplansky density package. [Task 3]\n- Preserve the dependency `P49` finite-stage/C*-corner trace → bicommutant/Kaplansky bounded approximation → `P50` faithful normal trace on `qMq` → `P51` finiteness/fullness. The finiteness calculation needs `τ_q(q-vv*)=0`; `q-v*v` is identically zero when `v*v=q`. Initial ready packets were `P47, P48, P52, P54`; recheck live state before relying on that snapshot. [Task 3]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- symptom: a short-range manuscript argument is promoted to the full regional theorem -> cause: coherent-coordinate and analytic hypotheses are missing -> fix: state the result conditionally or retain the analytic obligations explicitly. [Task 2]\n- symptom: Lean axioms are used to mask completion/normality/classification gaps -> fix: do not hide them; resume only with concrete gLU/refinement data, approval for a strengthened conditional theorem, or a deliberate infrastructure project. [Task 2]\n- symptom: strong closedness is treated as density of the original C*-algebra -> fix: distinguish retention of limits in `M` from bounded approximants supplied by Kaplansky density. An attempted P49A/P49B/P49C plan patch failed context matching, so inspect `PLAN.md`, TOML, and `state.json` and make a narrow verified update before claiming those packets exist. Recheck `aristotle-autopilot.timer` after any queue migration. [Task 3]\n\n# Task Group: <original-home>/Projects/current/homepage type-theoretic scientific paper formalization design\n\nscope: theory-first design of a companion typed term-and-inference representation for one of the user's scientific papers, distinct from blog prose, JSON prototypes, and provenance-only graphs\napplies_to: cwd=<original-home>/Projects/current/homepage; reuse_rule=reuse as a conceptual starting point for paper-formalization design; do not treat it as an implemented format, formal proof, or settled serialization schema\n\n## Task 1: establish the term-and-inference calculus foundation\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T20-52-01-QqoJ-type_theoretic_paper_formalization_system.md (cwd=<original-home>/Projects/current/homepage, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T22-52-01-019fc43f-76a9-7583-95b0-ba99f759f845.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-02T21:43:20+00:00, thread_id=019fc43f-76a9-7583-95b0-ba99f759f845, partial: theory discussion; no implementation)\n\nthread_id: 019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2\nupdated_at: 2026-08-03T03:04:54+00:00\nrollout_path: <original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T21-10-40-019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2.jsonl\ncwd: source-workspace\ngit_branch: master\n\n# Standalone Lean formalization of the stabilizer tensor-product theorem was advanced but not completed\n\nRollout context: The user requested formalization outside the Overleaf repository, first asking for a plan and approval. After approval, work proceeded in `lean/stabilizer`, leaving the Overleaf checkout untouched.\n\n## Task 1: Audit the manuscript theorem and define the formalization target\n\nOutcome: partial\n\nPreference signals:\n- The user explicitly requested a new folder rather than editing the Overleaf repo and asked the assistant to explain the intended target before acting -> future work should preserve the separate-project boundary and approval-gated setup.\n- The user said the manuscript proof “doesn't have to be the existing proof” because it may contain errors -> treat manuscript claims as proposed source claims requiring mathematical audit, not as authoritative premises.\n- The user specifically added “the existence of a tracial state induced by this tensor product” -> formalization must track state existence separately from algebraic isomorphism and factor classification.\n\nReusable knowledge:\n- The manuscript theorem claims a regional algebra isomorphic to `B(H) \\bar⊗ R`, with `R` hyperfinite `II₁`, but its proof leaves the infinite Pauli isomorphism, phase/coherence construction, product-state factorization, C*-extension, GNS/quasi-equivalence, and weak-closure identification unproved.\n- A key correction was established: if `H` is finite-dimensional, the tensor product can carry a faithful normal tracial state; if `H` is infinite-dimensional, `B(H) \\bar⊗ R` has a faithful normal semifinite trace, not a tracial state, and is the `II_∞` case.\n- The current pinned mathlib environment has C*-algebra and basic `VonNeumannAlgebra` structures, but no complete API for infinite von Neumann tensor products, normal traces/states, hyperfiniteness, or factor classification.\n\nReferences:\n- Overleaf source: `writing/overleaf_prl_stabilizer_region_algebras/main.tex`, especially the short-range theorem around lines 1740–1752 and proof discussion around 1905–1995.\n- New project: `lean/stabilizer`.\n\n## Task 2: Build the standalone project and formalize algebraic trace transport\n\nOutcome: success\n\nKey steps:\n- Created a standalone Lean project with `lakefile.lean`, pinned `leanprover/lean4:v4.28.0`, README, blueprint, and `Formalization/TraceTransport.lean`.\n- Proved that a unital tracial functional pulls back along a `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- Extended the project with finite matrix/UHF trace infrastructure, algebraic direct-limit maps and states, phase-corrected Pauli-word equivalences, and pure/mixed coordinate state results.\n\nReusable knowledge:\n- The main checked algebraic theorem is `StabilizerHyperfinite.isUnitalTracial_pullback`; its axiom audit reports only standard Lean axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- `Formalization/AlgebraicLimitStarHom.lean` and `Formalization/AlgebraicLimitTraceTransport.lean` provide the algebraic direct-limit transport layer, but explicitly do not claim C*-continuity or normality.\n- `Formalization/CStarEquivExtension.lean` proves that a supplied complex `StarAlgEquiv` between C*-algebras is isometric and continuous in both directions, and that a continuous functional pulls back continuously. It does not construct the required completions.\n- `Formalization/CoherentPhaseQubitState.lean` proves the phase-weighted stabilizer expectation formula from coherent finite-stage data plus an explicit selected-Z membership hypothesis. Its adapted-coordinate variant reduces the geometric input to literal membership in `coordinateStabilizerSubmodule`.\n\nVerification:\n- `lake build` and focused module builds succeeded.\n- Blueprint `blueprints/001-tensor-product-trace.tex` compiled in two passes with `pdflatex`.\n- No `sorry`, `admit`, or user-declared `axiom` remained in the final checked formal sources at closeout; audited theorem dependencies used only standard Lean axioms.\n\nReferences:\n- `Formalization/TraceTransport.lean`\n- `Formalization/CoherentPhaseQubitState.lean`\n- `Formalization/FiniteQubitPauliSelection.lean`\n- `Formalization/CStarEquivExtension.lean`\n- `blueprints/001-tensor-product-trace.tex`\n- `README.md` and `PROGRESS.md`\n\n## Task 3: Complete the full regional hyperfinite-factor theorem\n\nOutcome: blocked\n\nFailures and how to do differently:\n- The full theorem could not honestly be completed because the source supplies only a local adapted basis, not the required exhaustion-compatible finite-stage coordinate maps, phase calibration, or regional stabilizer-membership construction.\n- Do not replace the missing C*-completion, normal GNS/quasi-equivalence, spatial bicommutant extension, or hyperfinite factor classification with axioms. Keep them explicit as analytic obligations or strengthen the theorem statement conditionally.\n\nReusable knowledge:\n- The remaining obligations are: (1) construct coherent finite-support symplectic/gLU data, (2) identify actual regional Pauli multipliers and phases, (3) construct the quasi-local C*-isomorphism/completion, (4) prove product-state factorization, and (5) prove normal/spatial identification of bicommutants and factor type.\n- The rollout ended with the goal marked blocked after the repeated obstruction was audited. Resumption requires concrete gLU/refinement data, approval to adopt the strengthened conditional theorem, or deliberate development of the missing von Neumann/GNS/hyperfinite library.\n\nReferences:\n- `PROGRESS.md` section “The exact theorem still to prove”.\n- `blueprints/001-tensor-product-trace.tex` analytic-obligations and conditional-theorem sections.\n- The exact user-facing closeout stated that the original Overleaf dirty state was left untouched and no Aristotle workflow was used.\n","exit_code":0,"status