t\n    37\tP54, P56R's recovered state declarations, P57A's locally ported ITP core, and\n    38\tthe checked GNS/bicommutant transport modules.\n    39\t\n    40\t## Acceptance criteria\n    41\t\n    42\t`lake build AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensorFactorization` succeeds without\n    43\tforbidden declarations. Separate constructed GNS facts from supplied spatial\n    44\tvon Neumann closure facts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba PLAN.md | sed -n '45,135p'\"","aggregated_output":"    45\tLane H gives an explicit factor theorem and, in the infinite-pure case, the\n    46\tconcrete faithful normal semifinite weight `Tr barTensor tau`. Lane G gives\n    47\tthe general no-central-type-III theorem. A final comparison theorem may show\n    48\tthat the Lane-H factor model satisfies the Lane-G finite-corner criterion, but\n    49\tthe two results remain logically independent.\n    50\t\n    51\t## Aristotle package sequence\n    52\t\n    53\t### Shared/central core\n    54\t\n    55\t| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n    56\t|---|---|---|\n    57\t| P47 | `CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` | Define center, central projections, finite projections, corners, central support, and fullness for the concrete von Neumann-algebra model. Prove only algebraic order/corner lemmas; no direct integral. |\n    58\t| P48 | `GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean` | Formalize the general-lattice exhaustion, local code projections, monotonicity, and the strong-limit projection `q`. If the stabilizer definitions do not imply a required limit fact, expose it as an auxiliary hypothesis. |\n    59\t| P49 | `FiniteCornerTrace.lean` | Derive finite-stage trace cyclicity and pass it to the compressed quasi-local C-star algebra. Keep finite codespace density data explicit. |\n    60\t| P49A | `StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean` | Develop the strong-operator convergence/closure API needed for concrete operator algebras; prove commutants and hence concrete von Neumann algebras are strongly closed. This is a proved infrastructure theorem, not an interface. |\n    61\t| P49B | `VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean` | Prove the analytic double-commutant theorem for a unital complex star subalgebra of bounded operators: its bicommutant is its strong-operator closure. Develop the required finite amplification/cyclic-subspace machinery locally when Mathlib lacks it. |\n    62\t| P49C | `KaplanskyDensity.lean` | Prove bounded/unit-ball Kaplansky density for the represented C-star algebra in its bicommutant and derive the compressed-corner approximation used by the manuscript. No supplied density interface is accepted. |\n    63\t| P50 | `NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` | Using P49 and P49C, prove traciality of `tau_q` on `q M_Gamma q` by bounded strong approximation, prove faithfulness, and establish the stronger concrete WOT-continuity certificate that P50U will translate into the standard ultraweak-normal interface. |\n    64\t| P50U | `UltraweakNormality.lean` | Define the concrete ultraweak topology from absolutely summable matrix-coefficient series, prove the ultraweak-to-WOT identity is continuous, and upgrade P50's WOT-continuity certificate to literal ultraweak normality. This is mandatory infrastructure and may not alias ultraweak topology to WOT/SOT/norm. |\n    65\t| P51 | `FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` | Prove `q` finite, prove fullness, and derive `0 != z ->` a nonzero finite projection in `z M_Gamma`; define/use the project-local type-III obstruction. |\n    66\t\n    67\t### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n    68\t\n    69\t| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n    70\t|---|---|---|\n    71\t| P52 | `CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean` | Build finite coordinate blocks and an exhaustion from local hyperbolic data. Audit whether finite support suffices; otherwise isolate the exact local-finiteness/coherence assumption. |\n    72\t| P53 | `LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` | Construct the finite stage maps, phase calibration, and coherent algebraic `alpha`; instantiate the existing direct-limit theorems without supplied stage equivalences. |\n    73\t| P54 | `UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` | Construct a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the dyadic algebra from finite stages; do not assume an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space. |\n    74\t| P55A | `LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean` | Construct, rather than assume, the finite-stage star equivalence from each P53 coordinate Pauli algebra to the corresponding finite dyadic matrix algebra, with explicit generator/phase formulas and norm control. |\n    75\t| P55B | `LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean` | Prove coherence of the P55A maps and identify the P53 source direct limit with the coordinate dyadic limit; prove the finite terminal-stage and infinite cofinal-UHF branches separately. |\n    76\t| P55C | `LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations.lean` | Transport the P54 faithful representation through P55B and P53 alpha, and construct the source and regional closed operator-range C-star algebras with faithful dense embeddings. |\n    77\t| P55D | `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean` | Extend the P53 algebraic alpha uniquely between the P55C concrete C-star closures and prove the inverse and dense-range identities. |\n    78\t| P56 | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Retired partial result: it proves the finite-word/algebraic state equality and conditional continuous-extension uniqueness, but does not prove C-star boundedness or positivity. |\n    79\t| P56R | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Recovery after P55D: construct the pure/mixed product C-star state from finite-dimensional density-matrix estimates, prove positivity/unitality and transport it through `alpha`; no supplied norm bound. |\n    80\t| P57A | `VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean` | Shared infrastructure: port and audit the proved finite-support vacuum-restricted infinite-tensor pre-Hilbert core from `bound_beating`; do not import external projects or package a completion as an axiom. |\n    81\t| P57 | `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` | After P54, P56R, and P57A, construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space tensor splitting and the spatial represented-algebra identification. |\n    82\t| P58 | `MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` | Construct/prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under project-local factor and normal-trace definitions. |\n    83\t| P59 | `LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean` | Transport P57--P58 to the regional algebra, prove trivial center, and state the finite-pure trace versus infinite-pure faithful-normal-semifinite-weight dichotomy. |\n    84\t\n    85\t### Optional strengthening/reconnection\n    86\t\n    87\t| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n    88\t|---|---|---|\n    89\t| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Retired partial attempt: it constructs a conditional extended-positive trace series and finite-compression certificate, but does not yet prove standard positive-cone semifiniteness. |\n    90\t| P60R | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Recovery: define the weight on the positive cone and prove standard semifiniteness using positive square roots and the finite comparison projections. |\n    91\t| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n    92\t\n    93\t## Initial parallel wave\n    94\t\n    95\tSubmit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\n    96\tand P54. Integrate and semantically audit them before submitting dependent\n    97\tpackets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\n    98\tthey are not evidence and must be re-scoped against this plan before reuse.\n    99\t\n   100\t## Non-negotiable gates\n   101\t\n   102\t1. No claim that `q M_Gamma q` has merely a semifinite weight when the\n   103\t   construction actually targets a finite faithful normal tracial state.\n   104\t2. No claim of a global trace/weight on `M_Gamma` from the finite-corner\n   105\t   theorem alone.\n   106\t3. No claim that a finite-dimensional subalgebra excludes type III; the proof\n   107\t   must produce a nonzero finite projection in every nonzero central summand.\n   108\t4. No claim that hyperbolic data imply a factor before the spatial tensor\n   109\t   factorization and factorhood of both factors are proved.\n   110\t5. Every manuscript-facing packet identifies an exact `main.tex` locator and\n   111\t   every extra analytic hypothesis appears as a named field, never an axiom.\n   112\t6. P49A--P49C are mandatory proved infrastructure. P50 may not replace the\n   113\t   bicommutant theorem or Kaplansky density by a supplied structure field; an\n   114\t   incomplete analytic package halts Lane G and triggers review.\n   115\t7. P50's WOT-continuity theorem is a mathematically stronger certificate but\n   116\t   is not itself the standard definition of normality. P50U must formalize the\n   117\t   actual ultraweak topology and checked comparison before the project reports\n   118\t   the corner state as ultraweak-normal in the formal interface. P51's\n   119\t   finiteness/fullness proof is logically independent because it uses only\n   120\t   traciality and faithfulness.\n   121\t8. The original P55 exhausted its remote budget without producing its\n   122\t   authorized Lean file. It is retired, not accepted. P55A--P55D replace it\n   123\t   and expose the previously missing bridge between P53's twisted-Pauli direct\n   124\t   limit and P54's dyadic UHF model. P56 may advance only after P55D is\n   125\t   integrated and audited.\n   126\t9. P56 is preserved as a partial artifact, not accepted evidence: its\n   127\t   `ProductStateBound` is an explicit missing C-star norm estimate and it has\n   128\t   no positivity theorem. P56R must derive the bound and positivity from the\n   129\t   finite-dimensional density-matrix data and P55D's concrete C-star model;\n   130\t   it may not use `ProductStateBound` in its final declarations or proofs.\n   131\t10. P57A may reuse the algorithmic finite-support construction in\n   132\t    `bound_beating/formalize_itp`, but only by an audited local port. It may\n   133\t    not import that separate project, copy its optional completion/axiom\n   134\t    wrappers, or claim a completed Hilbert tensor product before the quotient\n   135\t    and completion API is actually proved.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
