{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba PROGRESS.md | sed -n '1,300p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Formalization progress\n     2\t\n     3\t## Context policy (2026-08-05)\n     4\t\n     5\tAll future manuscript-facing formalization takes its context only from\n     6\t`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`, with exact locators in the manuscript `main.tex`. Earlier\n     7\tgLU/refinement/layer-coherence artifacts remain available only as explicitly\n     8\tlabelled legacy infrastructure; they are not manuscript hypotheses. See\n     9\t`AGENTS.md` and `CONTEXT-LEDGER.md`.\n    10\t\n    11\tThe manuscript-facing module sequence is now `Formalization.Manuscript`:\n    12\tsource boundary, finite model, algebraic limit, product state, conditional GNS\n    13\tbridge, trace dichotomy, and only then the pending theorem contract. Existing\n    14\timplementation files remain in place and are imported through facades.\n    15\t\n    16\t- P17 — under a supplied finite adapted-coordinate/word realization, the\n    17\t  finite pure/mixed product state is exactly the stabilizer indicator on every\n    18\t  supplied source Pauli basis word.\n    19\t- P18 — a supplied finite matrix-factor tensor decomposition transports the\n    20\t  finite product trace to an algebraic tracial state with its elementary-tensor\n    21\t  formula.\n    22\t- P19 — a supplied C-star model plus compatible states packages the existing\n    23\t  GNS unitary and algebraic commutant transport into one bridge interface.\n    24\t- P23 — supplied coherent finite-stage star equivalences induce the infinite\n    25\t  algebraic direct-limit regional equivalence `alpha`, with finite-stage and\n    26\t  inverse formulas. No C-star or von Neumann extension is claimed.\n    27\t- P24 — compatible target-stage algebraic states pull back along `alpha` to a\n    28\t  unique algebraic direct-limit state with its exact finite-stage expectation\n    29\t  formula and conditional stabilizer-indicator corollary.\n    30\t- P25 — supplied C-star completions and an extension of `alpha` yield an\n    31\t  isometric continuous C-star equivalence and continuous state pullback;\n    32\t  existence of those completions remains an explicit assumption.\n    33\t\n    34\t## Checked Lean results\n    35\t\n    36\t- `TPT-001` / `TPT-002` — an algebraic tracial state pulls back along a\n    37\t  complex `StarAlgEquiv`.\n    38\t- TPT-003 — algebraic traciality is reflected as well as preserved by a\n    39\t  complex star-algebra equivalence; hence a nontracial product state cannot\n    40\t  become tracial after an algebraic coordinate identification.\n    41\t- `FMT-001` — the normalized trace on a nonempty finite full matrix algebra is\n    42\t  an algebraic tracial state.  Positivity is proved by the explicit\n    43\t  trace-of-a-star-square sum-of-squares identity.\n    44\t- `FSC-001` — a finite corner equipped with a star isomorphism to a full matrix\n    45\t  algebra inherits that algebraic tracial state.\n    46\t- `FTT-001` — the finite algebraic tensor product of two matrix factors is\n    47\t  identified by the Kronecker star isomorphism, and its normalized trace\n    48\t  factorizes on elementary tensors; tensoring with a matrix identity preserves\n    49\t  the trace.\n    50\t- `FAM-001` — if `R` has an algebraic tracial state, then its finite matrix\n    51\t  amplification `Matrix n n R` has the normalized diagonal tracial state.\n    52\t  Positivity is checked as a finite sum of coefficient-algebra star-squares.\n    53\t  An explicit `StarAlgEquiv` transports this finite type-I product trace to a\n    54\t  target algebra.\n    55\t- `TMT-001` — the finite type-I product is now identified canonically, not\n    56\t  supplied as an assumption: `Matrix n n ℂ ⊗[ℂ] R` is star-isomorphic to\n    57\t  `Matrix n n R`.  Its trace factors on elementary tensors as the normalized\n    58\t  matrix trace times the coefficient trace.\n    59\t- `DTT-001` — the actual dyadic finite-stage system is constructed as\n    60\t  `A₀ = ℂ`, `Aₙ₊₁ = Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) Aₙ`, with diagonal identity-qubit\n    61\t  embeddings.  Its normalized traces are compatible with every stage map,\n    62\t  and their algebraic directed limit carries the induced algebraic tracial\n    63\t  state.\n    64\t- FPU-001 — for every nonempty finite matrix factor, its algebraic tensor\n    65\t  product with the concrete dyadic algebraic limit carries the checked product\n    66\t  tracial state.  The theorem includes the elementary-tensor formula\n    67\t  tr_p(a) times qubitUHFTrace(u).\n    68\t- FPU-002 — any supplied regional `StarAlgEquiv` into that finite-pure\n    69\t  product model induces an algebraic tracial state on the regional algebra,\n    70\t  with the checked formula on inverse images of elementary tensors.\n    71\t- `AIT-001` — compatible unital cyclic finite-stage functionals glue to a\n    72\t  unital cyclic linear functional on mathlib's algebraic directed direct\n    73\t  limit.\n    74\t- `AIT-002` — compatible stagewise star-algebra maps induce an involutive,\n    75\t  additive, multiplication-reversing star on that algebraic direct limit.\n    76\t  Compatible algebraic tracial states then glue to an ordinary algebraic\n    77\t  tracial state there.\n    78\t- `SPC-001` — an adapted Hamel basis identifies the label space with finitely\n    79\t  supported X/Z coordinate labels and maps the singleton coordinate labels to\n    80\t  the chosen basis vectors.\n    81\t- ASC-001 — for a selected set of Z coordinates, Lean now identifies the\n    82\t  corresponding coordinate subspace both as the span of those Z basis\n    83\t  vectors and as the finite words with no X coordinate and no Z coordinate\n    84\t  outside the selected set.  This is the exact linear selection criterion\n    85\t  required before comparing the regional stabilizer state with the\n    86\t  pure/mixed product state.\n    87\t- FQS-001 — Lean now reads the recursive finite-qubit Pauli label as its\n    88\t  finite X/Z coordinate list and proves that the pure/mixed product-state\n    89\t  indicator is exactly the selected-Z condition: a pure coordinate has no X\n    90\t  exponent, and a mixed coordinate is the identity label.  Under an arbitrary\n    91\t  supplied adapted coordinate basis, that condition is literal membership in\n    92\t  the selected-Z stabilizer submodule.  The coherent direct-limit state theorem\n    93\t  has a corresponding selected-Z indicator form on source basis words.\n    94\t- `PCC-001` — a phase-corrected additive map of Pauli labels respects word\n    95\t  multiplication and star exactly when it satisfies explicit multiplier and\n    96\t  involution equations.  This isolates the cocycle data that symplecticity\n    97\t  alone does not supply.  The cross-algebra word-basis extension is now also\n    98\t  checked: its two compatibility equations and a specified Pauli-word basis\n    99\t  yield a genuine `StarAlgEquiv`.\n   100\t- `SCC-001` — the quotient of two multiplier phases is an additive character,\n   101\t  calibrating by an additive character preserves the multiplier equation, and\n   102\t  every additive character on a vector subspace extends to the ambient vector\n   103\t  space along a complementary subspace.  This is the exact algebraic\n   104\t  stabilizer-sign calibration: the finite-field character is self-conjugate,\n   105\t  and calibration preserves both Pauli-word compatibility equations.  The\n   106\t  concrete finite-support quadratic phase is now independently formalized;\n   107\t  relating it to the actual regional stabilizer convention remains separate.\n   108\t- QPR-001 — the explicit ZMod 4 finite-support quadratic refinement has its\n   109\t  polarization and diagonal identities fully checked.  Its discrepancy pairing\n   110\t  is additive in both words, symmetric for a symmetric discrepancy, and has\n   111\t  additive order two.  These facts instantiate the cross-algebra Pauli-word\n   112\t  multiplication and involution certificates and, with a supplied word-basis\n   113\t  linear equivalence, a `StarAlgEquiv`.\n   114\t- QPT-001 — the concrete finite-support phase theorem now composes that\n   115\t  `StarAlgEquiv` with the finite-pure times qubit-UHF trace transport: whenever\n   116\t  the regional Pauli-word exponents, involution phases, and word-basis map are\n   117\t  supplied, Lean constructs both the star-algebra equivalence and its induced\n   118\t  algebraic tracial state with the elementary-tensor product formula.  The\n   119\t  Pauli-word interface has been weakened from `Ring` to `Semiring`, the exact\n   120\t  structure carried by the concrete algebraic UHF direct limit.\n   121\t- PTO-001 — two isometries whose range projections sum to the identity rule\n   122\t  out even an algebraic unital cyclic trace.  This is the checked obstruction\n   123\t  behind the infinite-pure-sector case; the tracial-state theorem is therefore\n   124\t  deliberately limited to a finite pure matrix factor.\n   125\t- ALT-001 — compatible finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv`s and compatible target\n   126\t  algebraic tracial states induce a source-side algebraic tracial state on the\n   127\t  corresponding quasi-local direct limit.  The theorem evaluates it exactly\n   128\t  on every finite-stage representative.  The concrete finite-pure UHF trace\n   129\t  now has the matching finite-stage elementary-tensor formula.\n   130\t- FQP-001 — every finite stage of the dyadic qubit tower now has an explicit\n   131\t  ordered Pauli-word `StarSystem` and a complex Pauli-word basis.  The\n   132\t  identity-qubit embeddings preserve its words, basis vectors, multiplication\n   133\t  multipliers, and star multipliers under coherent label maps.  Thus the UHF\n   134\t  target-side finite-stage word hypotheses are no longer abstract assumptions;\n   135\t  assembling them into one global target word system remains open.\n   136\t- PMS-001 — for every Boolean sequence specifying whether each newly adjoined\n   137\t  qubit is pure or maximally mixed, the corresponding finite product\n   138\t  functionals are algebraic states, are compatible with all dyadic embeddings,\n   139\t  and induce an algebraic state on the UHF direct limit.  Their values on every\n   140\t  finite Pauli word are proved recursively: pure coordinates permit only zero\n   141\t  X exponent, while mixed coordinates permit only the identity word.  The\n   142\t  all-mixed specialization is proved equal to the previously checked UHF\n   143\t  tracial state.  Lean also proves that even the one-qubit pure specialization\n   144\t  is not cyclic and hence not an algebraic tracial state.\n   145\t- PTR-001 — this nontraciality is now proved at arbitrary finite and\n   146\t  direct-limit coordinates: if any Boolean coordinate is pure, explicit\n   147\t  matrix units witness a failure of cyclicity.  Consequently the algebraic\n   148\t  UHF product state is tracial if and only if every coordinate is maximally\n   149\t  mixed, in which case it is the checked UHF trace.\n   150\t- CBL-001 — finite-stage star-algebra equivalences need not be assumed\n   151\t  coherent on every algebra element: if the source connecting maps, target\n   152\t  vectors, and coordinate maps agree on a specified source basis, Lean proves\n   153\t  the full commuting square by linear-basis extensionality.\n   154\t- CPS-001 — a phase-corrected finite coordinate system now has a concrete\n   155\t  direct-limit state interface.  Coherent source basis transport, phases, and\n   156\t  finite Pauli labels imply full-stage equivalence coherence and hence a\n   157\t  star-algebra equivalence to the algebraic qubit-UHF direct limit; the induced\n   158\t  source state evaluates a basis word as its phase times the pure/mixed Pauli\n   159\t  selection indicator.  The all-mixed specialization pulls the UHF trace back\n   160\t  to a source algebraic tracial state; more generally its pure/mixed pullback\n   161\t  is tracial exactly when every coordinate is mixed.  Constructing the\n   162\t  regional inputs remains open.\n   163\t- ACS-001 — if supplied finite-stage regional data identify selected target\n   164\t  Z-coordinates with the actual source stabilizer words, Lean derives the\n   165\t  exact phase-calibrated stabilizer expectation formula on every source basis word.\n   166\t  The stronger form states that hypothesis as literal membership in the\n   167\t  selected-Z submodule of an adapted coordinate basis.  Thus the remaining\n   168\t  geometric work is isolated to constructing and coherently transporting that\n   169\t  coordinate data from a separately supplied finite-coordinate realization,\n   170\t  rather than to a hidden infinite-algebra assumption. The manuscript does not\n   171\t  presently supply that realization; see `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`.\n   172\t- ALS-001 — compatible finite-stage star-algebra equivalences transport\n   173\t  compatible algebraic states (not only tracial states) to a quasi-local\n   174\t  algebraic direct limit.  This is the exact state-level interface required by\n   175\t  a coherent regional stabilizer-coordinate construction.\n   176\t- WBE-001 — if Pauli words form a complex linear basis, checking a\n   177\t  complex-linear map on every pair of basis words proves multiplicativity on\n   178\t  all finite sums.  The corresponding conjugate-linear basis argument proves\n   179\t  star preservation; a bijective unital map satisfying both checks is packaged\n   180\t  as a star-algebra equivalence.\n   181\t- ALC-001 — a compatible family of finite-stage star-algebra maps induces a\n   182\t  star-algebra map from the algebraic directed limit.  Compatible finite-stage\n   183\t  star-algebra equivalences induce a star-algebra equivalence of the two\n   184\t  algebraic limits.  The C-star norm extension remains open.\n   185\t- CSE-001 — once a source and target are supplied as complex C-star algebras,\n   186\t  Lean proves that every complex `StarAlgEquiv` is isometric and therefore\n   187\t  continuous with continuous inverse.  A continuous target functional pulls\n   188\t  back continuously along it.  This does not construct C-star norms or\n   189\t  completions for the algebraic direct-limit models.\n   190\t- CCF-001 — the pinned Mathlib supports the finite dyadic stages as genuine\n   191\t  C-star algebras and supports closure/minimality once an ambient C-star\n   192\t  algebra is supplied.  It does not provide the C-star inductive-limit\n   193\t  construction for the algebraic dyadic limit; this is recorded as an\n   194\t  explicit missing API rather than hidden behind an axiom.\n   195\t- NMC-001 — supplied finite C-star realizations of the coherent coordinate\n   196\t  maps are isometric and continuous, and the commuting inclusion squares\n   197\t  preserve the norm estimates.  The resulting dense-subalgebra estimate is\n   198\t  exactly the analytic input needed before extending the algebraic map to a\n   199\t  completion; no completion is constructed here.\n   200\t- BMC-001 — for a star subalgebra of bounded operators on a Hilbert space,\n   201\t  Lean now constructs the algebraic bicommutant as a concrete\n   202\t  `VonNeumannAlgebra`, with monotonicity, minimality, membership, and\n   203\t  idempotence lemmas.  The analytic strong/weak double-commutant theorem is\n   204\t  still explicitly absent from the pinned Mathlib and remains separate.\n   205\t- CCC-001 — from an explicitly supplied isometric star representation of a\n   206\t  pre-C-star algebra into bounded operators, Lean constructs the closed\n   207\t  operator-range C-star algebra, its isometric dense embedding, and the\n   208\t  uniqueness equivalence between two such concrete completions.  The faithful\n   209\t  operator representation of the project-specific algebraic limit is still a\n   210\t  separate obligation.\n   211\t\n   212\t## The exact theorem still to prove\n   213\t\n   214\tThe Overleaf short-range theorem asserts a regional von Neumann algebra\n   215\tisomorphism to a type-I factor tensor a hyperfinite type-II1 factor.  It is\n   216\tnot yet formalized as a theorem because the supplied manuscript proof leaves\n   217\tthe following essential premises open:\n   218\t\n   219\t1. a finite-support adapted symplectic coordinate map whose finite-stage\n   220\t   source bases, phase correction, and target Pauli labels are coherent along\n   221\t   an exhaustion;\n   222\t2. identification of the actual regional Pauli multiplier and involution\n   223\t   exponents with the finite-support coordinate discrepancy, followed by\n   224\t   calibration to the actual stabilizer character;\n   225\t3. the induced quasi-local C-star isomorphism;\n   226\t4. factorization of the regional state into pure and normalized-tracial\n   227\t   coordinate states; and\n   228\t5. a normal/spatial extension to the respective bicommutants.\n   229\t\n   230\tThe current pinned mathlib version includes preliminary abstract and concrete\n   231\tvon Neumann-algebra definitions, but lacks a finished API for infinite von\n   232\tNeumann tensor products, normal states/traces, hyperfiniteness, and factor\n   233\tclassification.  The project therefore does not introduce any axiom for the\n   234\ttarget theorem.\n   235\t\n   236\t## Last verification\n   237\t\n   238\t```text\n   239\tlake build\n   240\tlake build Formalization.AlgebraicLimitStateTransport Formalization.QubitMatrixState Formalization.FinitePureMixedQubitState Formalization\n   241\tlake build Formalization.TraceTransport Formalization\n   242\tlake build Formalization.CoherentBasisEquiv Formalization.CoherentPhaseQubitState Formalization\n   243\tlake build Formalization.PureCoordinateNotTracial Formalization\n   244\tlake build Formalization.AdaptedStabilizerSubspace Formalization\n   245\tlake build Formalization.FiniteQubitPauliSelection Formalization.CoherentPhaseQubitState Formalization\n   246\tlake build Formalization.CStarEquivExtension Formalization\n   247\tlake build AristotleCandidates.CStarInductiveLimitFeasibility AristotleCandidates.FiniteCoordinateMapNormControl\n   248\tlake env lean /tmp/stabilizer_hyperfinite_axioms_run4.lean\n   249\tpdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error .../001-tensor-product-trace.tex\n   250\t```\n   251\t\n   252\tLean reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound` for the\n   253\tchecked tensor-amplification, concrete dyadic direct-limit trace,\n   254\tfinite-support quadratic-phase, induced-trace, finite-qubit Pauli-word,\n   255\tpure/mixed product-state, basis-level coherence, phase-corrected direct-limit\n   256\tequivalence/state transport, and properly-infinite trace-obstruction theorems.\n   257\tNo source theorem contains `sorry`, `admit`, or a user-declared axiom.  The\n   258\tblueprint build output is kept under `/tmp`, not in this source project.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
