{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md | sed -n '1,180p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Two-lane formalization decision\n     2\t\n     3\tDate: 2026-08-07\n     4\t\n     5\tThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n     6\t\n     7\t**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\n     8\tthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\n     9\ton `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\n    10\tnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\n    11\tIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\n    12\ttrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n    13\t\n    14\t**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\n    15\tcoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\n    16\tidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\n    17\ttrace/weight classification.\n    18\t\n    19\tThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\n    20\ttensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\n    21\tcase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\n    22\twithout asserting trivial center.\n    23\t\n    24\tThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\n    25\tdependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\n    26\tintegrated and semantically audited.\n    27\t\n    28\tAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\n    29\tC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\n    30\tAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\n    31\talgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\n    32\tunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\n    33\tboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\n    34\tanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\n    35\treplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n    36\t\n    37\tAmendment, 2026-08-08: P50's checked WOT continuity is retained as a stronger\n    38\tconcrete certificate, but the field name alone is not accepted as a\n    39\tformalization of the standard ultraweak definition of normality. Package P50U\n    40\tmust define the ultraweak topology from absolutely summable series of matrix\n    41\tcoefficients, prove the topology comparison, and export an explicitly\n    42\tultraweak-normal P50 conclusion. This does not block P51's finite-projection\n    43\targument, which uses the corner state's traciality and faithfulness rather than\n    44\tnormality.\n    45\t\n    46\tAmendment, 2026-08-08: the original P55 is retired after Aristotle returned\n    47\t`OUT_OF_BUDGET` without creating `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`. The failed\n    48\trun is not evidence and no code from it is integrated. Lane H now uses four\n    49\tseparate gates: P55A constructs finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic equivalences,\n    50\tP55B proves coherence and the finite/infinite direct-limit identifications,\n    51\tP55C constructs faithful source/regional operator representations and their\n    52\tclosed ranges, and P55D extends the algebraic alpha by density. This split is\n    53\tmathematical: P53 and P54 did not yet contain an identification between their\n    54\ttwo different algebraic direct limits. P56 depends on accepted P55D.\n    55\t\n    56\tP60 may run independently of Lane H after P51 and P50U. It is optional Lane-G\n    57\tstrengthening and must use P50U's literal ultraweak-normal corner state. It may\n    58\tassume an explicitly named countable comparison family for the full corner,\n    59\tbut it may not infer a global weight from fullness alone or conceal the weight,\n    60\tnormality, faithfulness, traciality, or semifiniteness laws in an axiom.\n    61\t\n    62\tAmendment, 2026-08-08: P60 compiled and its conditional weight-series,\n    63\ttraciality, faithfulness, corner restriction, and finite-compression results\n    64\tare preserved, but P60 is not accepted as the optional global-weight theorem.\n    65\tThe closeout's P51 provenance objection was stale: P51 is accepted in\n    66\t`reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md`. The genuine\n    67\tremaining gap is standard semifiniteness on the positive cone. P60R may revise\n    68\tthe P60 candidate in place, but must prove that for each nonzero positive\n    69\t`x ∈ M` there is a nonzero positive `y ≤ x` of finite weight. It must construct\n    70\tthe required positive square-root/factorization argument from Mathlib or\n    71\tlocal proved C-star theory; that factorization may not be a new hypothesis.\n    72\t\n    73\tAmendment, 2026-08-10: P56 is retained as a partial, reviewed artifact. Its\n    74\tfinite-word and algebraic direct-limit identities are useful, but its concrete\n    75\textensions depend on `ProductStateBound` and no positivity theorem was proved.\n    76\tP56R replaces it as the Lane-H state gate and must derive a genuine unital\n    77\tpositive C-star functional directly from the finite pure/mixed density-matrix\n    78\tdata and the P55D concrete alpha. The original P56 job is disabled rather than\n    79\trewritten, so the distinction remains machine-visible.\n    80\t\n    81\tIn parallel, P57A ports the *proved* finite-support vacuum-restricted infinite\n    82\ttensor pre-Hilbert construction from the compatible Lean-4.28 `bound_beating`\n    83\tworkspace into this repository as shared infrastructure. This is a local port,\n    84\tnot a cross-project import. Its optional completion/axiom wrapper is explicitly\n    85\texcluded: P57A can establish the algebraic kernel, finite-mode realization,\n    86\tpositivity, sesquilinearity, and pre-inner-product core, but the completed\n    87\tHilbert-space and spatial tensor claims remain P57 work and must be proved\n    88\tagainst the local Mathlib API.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
