hence a\n   157\t  star-algebra equivalence to the algebraic qubit-UHF direct limit; the induced\n   158\t  source state evaluates a basis word as its phase times the pure/mixed Pauli\n   159\t  selection indicator.  The all-mixed specialization pulls the UHF trace back\n   160\t  to a source algebraic tracial state; more generally its pure/mixed pullback\n   161\t  is tracial exactly when every coordinate is mixed.  Constructing the\n   162\t  regional inputs remains open.\n   163\t- ACS-001 — if supplied finite-stage regional data identify selected target\n   164\t  Z-coordinates with the actual source stabilizer words, Lean derives the\n   165\t  exact phase-calibrated stabilizer expectation formula on every source basis word.\n   166\t  The stronger form states that hypothesis as literal membership in the\n   167\t  selected-Z submodule of an adapted coordinate basis.  Thus the remaining\n   168\t  geometric work is isolated to constructing and coherently transporting that\n   169\t  coordinate data from a separately supplied finite-coordinate realization,\n   170\t  rather than to a hidden infinite-algebra assumption. The manuscript does not\n   171\t  presently supply that realization; see `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`.\n   172\t- ALS-001 — compatible finite-stage star-algebra equivalences transport\n   173\t  compatible algebraic states (not only tracial states) to a quasi-local\n   174\t  algebraic direct limit.  This is the exact state-level interface required by\n   175\t  a coherent regional stabilizer-coordinate construction.\n   176\t- WBE-001 — if Pauli words form a complex linear basis, checking a\n   177\t  complex-linear map on every pair of basis words proves multiplicativity on\n   178\t  all finite sums.  The corresponding conjugate-linear basis argument proves\n   179\t  star preservation; a bijective unital map satisfying both checks is packaged\n   180\t  as a star-algebra equivalence.\n   181\t- ALC-001 — a compatible family of finite-stage star-algeb