{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' reviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md && sed -n '1,260p' reviews/P56R-regional-cstar-product-state-closeout.md && sed -n '1,240p' reviews/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-closeout.md\"","aggregated_output":"# P54 closeout review — faithful UHF reference representation\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure-only Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P54-uhf-reference-representation.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`2843359fff4021ff2350373fd8ec82c3ffd0948ccf723193b5bc996a0d084668`) and\nextracted, without building, updating, or fetching dependencies, at\n`aristotle_responses/P54-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p54-0ps3ce65_aristotle/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` was integrated into the\nlive project.  Its SHA-256 is\n`786a1b2b89bf14eb61cf7f703ea646d095d3d640ac20b814c012a6e82b1c8eb9` in both\nlocations.  The archive and extraction remain raw response records.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe module imports only the pre-existing, byte-identical live modules\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`,\n`AristotleCandidates.AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation`, and\n`AristotleCandidates.ConcreteCStarCompletion`.\n\nIt constructs the following principal declarations:\n\n- `UHFL2`, `uhfL2Core`, and `UHFGNS`, the trace-GNS pre-Hilbert space of\n  `QubitUHFAlgebra` and its `UniformSpace.Completion`;\n- `qubitTensorPower_exists_bound`, `qubitUHF_exists_bound`,\n  `qubitUHFTrace_faithful`, and `uhfNormSq_mul_le`;\n- `uhfRep : QubitUHFAlgebra →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)`, together with\n  `uhfRep_injective`, `uhfCyclicVector_norm`, and\n  `uhfRep_vector_state`;\n- the compatible finite-stage family `uhfStageRep` and\n  `uhfRepData : QubitOperatorRepresentationData UHFGNS`, with\n  `uhfStageRep_compat`, `uhfRepData_rho_injective`,\n  `uhfRepData_limitRep`, and `uhfRepData_limitRep_injective`; and\n- the concrete closed operator-range C-star algebra `UHFConcreteCStar` with\n  its injective dense embedding `uhfConcreteEmbedding` and\n  `uhfConcreteEmbedding_denseRange`.\n\nThere are **no supplied auxiliary assumptions**: boundedness is established\nfrom the internal algebraic sum-of-squares cone `sumSqCone` and the finite\ndyadic matrix tower; faithfulness comes from the constructed canonical trace.\nThe Hilbert space is a completion of that pre-Hilbert space, not an assumed\ninfinite tensor-product Hilbert space.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The module constructs a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the algebraic dyadic limit, including injective finite-stage representations and the induced-limit identification. |\n| partial | The concrete closure is an operator-range C-star model, but P54 deliberately does not identify it with a project-specific regional completion or prove a spatial tensor-product model. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks the P54 gate. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated scope.  The additional\nclosed operator-range C-star construction is supporting infrastructure and\ndoes not weaken or replace the requested faithful reference representation.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P54, Lane H.\n- **Predecessors:** none.  The packet is one of the four explicitly approved\n  independent foundation packages.  Its three imports are prior local\n  infrastructure, not P47--P61 dependencies, and were byte-identical in the\n  quarantine snapshot and live checkout.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator\n  representation of the dyadic algebraic limit is constructed from finite\n  stages, without assuming an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The candidate neither defines\n  a regional alpha nor proves a state identity for a regional algebra, a\n  spatial tensor product, factorhood/type, or a trace/weight classification.\n  Its trace-GNS vector-state identity concerns only the constructed dyadic\n  reference representation and is not such a classification claim.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation` — passed in\n  the live project.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation Formalization`\n  — passed in the live project.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `lake env lean AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` —\n  passed.  Because the new untracked module was not emitted as an `.olean` by\n  the package target, the same live source was explicitly compiled with\n  `lake env lean -o .lake/build/lib/lean/AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.olean ...`\n  before importing it for the axiom report.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for\n  `qubitTensorPower_exists_bound`, `qubitUHFTrace_faithful`,\n  `uhfNormSq_mul_le`, `uhfRep`, `uhfRep_injective`, `uhfStageRep_compat`,\n  `uhfRepData_limitRep_injective`, and `uhfConcreteEmbedding_denseRange` —\n  each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate and direct imports — no\n  `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or\n  `native_decide` occurrence.  Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and\n  `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The review checked that the completion is\nexplicitly the trace-GNS completion rather than an infinite tensor product;\nthat the bounded left action is proved from the algebraic cone bound rather\nthan supplied as a completion/isometry interface; that the finite-stage\ncompatibility and limit faithfulness are actual declarations; and that the\ncandidate does not cross into P55--P59 regional, spatial, factor, or\ntrace/weight claims.  Lean compilation and axiom reports validate this\nformal infrastructure only; they do not establish any manuscript statement\nor later analytic tensor-factor conclusion.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P54 candidate, the raw quarantine archive\nand extraction, this closeout review, and the generated live `.olean` cache\nunder the existing `.lake/build/` tree.  All pre-existing modified and\nuntracked work was preserved.  No manuscript file was changed; no commit,\npush, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n# P56R closeout review — recovered regional C-star product state\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated conditional Lane-H scope; queue may advance.**\n\nAristotle project `026bfc92-1158-49a3-9049-ca7588e54dbb`, task\n`91db2acf-a167-41cd-bebd-ef882f843c64`, is terminal `COMPLETE` in\n`history/logs/20260810T080459Z-026bfc92-tasks.log`.\nThe supervisor-supplied archive\n`aristotle_responses/P56R-regional-cstar-product-state-026bfc92-91db2acf.tar.gz`\nhas SHA-256\n`09c401cad7ea05da5257575b5a4a019bed4fdb802833e3a95e2e70f14f75ba1a`.\nIt was extracted only into\n`aristotle_responses/P56R-regional-cstar-product-state-026bfc92-91db2acf-quarantine/`;\nno Lean build, dependency update, or dependency fetch ran there.  The only\npacket-owned source integrated into the live project was\n`AristotleCandidates/RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean`.  Its live SHA-256\nmatches the quarantined candidate exactly:\n\n```text\na2a4cbcc0aabdf90da9de9b75d15a60bc6c8dff7c5f12a5d7f5a56f2a76b5f00\n```\n\nNo manuscript, P55D predecessor, unrelated candidate, or unrelated dirty file\nwas modified.  The older P56 material remains in the same candidate as a\npreserved partial artifact; it is not evidence for the P56R acceptance.\n\n## Exact P56R declarations and assumptions\n\nThe recovery section adds the following proved declarations:\n\n- `AlphaData.norm_stageProductState_le`: the finite-stage product functional\n  is norm-decreasing for the finite matrix C-star norm.\n- `AlphaData.stageProductState_positive`: every finite-stage value on\n  `star x * x` is a nonnegative real.\n- `AlphaData.sourceProductState_positive` and\n  `AlphaData.sourceProductState_isAlgebraicState`: positivity and unitality\n  on the algebraic direct limit.\n- `AlphaData.norm_sourceEmbedding_sourceOf` and\n  `SourceConcreteRep.norm_sourceProductState_le`: the stage and direct-limit\n  estimates transported through the faithful isometric P55C embedding.\n- `SourceConcreteRep.cstarProductStateRecovered`, together with\n  `cstarProductStateRecovered_sourceEmbedding`,\n  `cstarProductStateRecovered_one`,\n  `cstarProductStateRecovered_positive`,\n  `cstarProductStateRecovered_isAlgebraicState`, and\n  `norm_cstarProductStateRecovered_le_one`: the continuous source C-star\n  functional, its dense formula, unitality, positivity on every square, local\n  state predicate, and norm bound.\n- `SourceConcreteRep.cstarRegionalStateRecovered`, together with\n  `cstarRegionalStateRecovered_targetEmbedding`,\n  `cstarRegionalStateRecovered_one`,\n  `cstarRegionalStateRecovered_positive`, and\n  `cstarRegionalStateRecovered_isAlgebraicState`: the transported regional\n  functional and its corresponding properties.\n- `SourceConcreteRep.cstarRegionalStateRecovered_cstarAlpha` and\n  `cstarRegionalStateRecovered_comp_cstarAlpha`: the required exact\n  alpha-transport identity.\n\nP56R adds no auxiliary premise.  It takes an `A : AlphaData L I` and an\n`R : A.SourceConcreteRep`, hence inherits only the already explicit P53/P55D\nconditional infrastructure: the P52 local-hyperbolic family and lattice\nexhaustion, `[LinearOrder I]`, and the named `AlphaData.symplectic` and\n`AlphaData.stage_surjective` assumptions, together with the constructed\nP55C finite/infinite concrete representation branch and the checked finite\npure/mixed one-qubit data.  No `ProductStateBound`, supplied positivity,\nsupplied state, supplied completion, or new axiom is used by any recovery\ndeclaration.\n\nThe local predicate is the existing project predicate\n`StabilizerHyperfinite.IsAlgebraicState`: unitality plus positivity on\n`star x * x`.  All fields are proved; no standard von Neumann normality claim\nis being smuggled into this predicate.\n\n## Changed proof route\n\nP56R replaces the old conditional `ProductStateBound` route with a proved\nfinite-dimensional density-matrix route.  It constructs the allowed-stage\ndensity matrix\n`D = ∑ v ∈ allowedStage, pauliMat v`, proves `D† = D`, `D² = |G| D`, and\ncomputes its trace.  A column decomposition of `tr (D x D)` proves both the\nfinite-stage norm estimate and positivity.  The estimate transports through\nthe injective star homomorphism into the P55C concrete C-star model, after\nwhich a proved dense continuous extension supplies the source functional and\ntransport through `cstarAlpha.symm` supplies the regional functional.\n\nThis is an alternative proof route, not a weakened target: it adds no premise\nand does not reuse the preserved §8 `ProductStateBound` declarations in the\nP56R recovery results.\n\n## Acceptance classification\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The complete P56R gate is proved: finite-stage norm/positivity, algebraic state, continuous source C-star state, transported regional state, and exact alpha identity. |\n| partial | Relative to the manuscript theorem, the result remains conditional on P55D’s explicit coordinate and concrete-model data. The manuscript source does not itself construct those hypotheses. |\n| blocked | None at the P56R gate. GNS tensor splitting, spatial von Neumann tensor products, factorhood, and trace/weight classification remain later packages and were not attempted. |\n| failed | None. No compilation, placeholder, archive-integrity, or scope failure was found. |\n\nThe packet’s mathematical target is therefore met at its stated scope.  It is\nnot a claim that the full manuscript theorem is established.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P56R`, Lane `H`; correct.\n- **Predecessors:** `P55D` is integrated, live-compiled, and semantically\n  audited in `reviews/P55D-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-closeout.md`.  The\n  original `P56` is explicitly retained as a partial artifact and was not\n  treated as a predecessor.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged exactly: construct the pure/mixed product\n  C-star state and prove its equality with the regional state transported by\n  the exact P55D C-star `alpha`.\n- **Forbidden claims:** respected.  No GNS tensor splitting, von Neumann\n  spatial tensor product, factorhood, center/trivial-center theorem, or\n  trace/weight classification occurs in the recovery section.\n\nThe source basis in the packet is `main.tex:1921-1946`, matching the\nmanuscript’s proposed state construction and finite-word identity.  The\nmanuscript-facing geometric coordinate/model hypotheses remain external\nconditional infrastructure, as required by `AGENTS.md` and\n`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity` — passed\n  (`8096/8096` jobs).\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity Formalization`\n  — passed (`8096/8096` jobs).\n- `lake build` — passed; the full live project was up to date.\n- `#print axioms` for all load-bearing recovery declarations listed above —\n  each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder scan of the candidate and direct P55D/finite-pure-mixed imports\n  — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Recovery-section scan — no forbidden downstream terms or declarations.\n- Live/quarantine candidate hash comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n- The exact archive was inspected and extracted without building inside the\n  dependency-free quarantine snapshot.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The review checked that the finite estimate\ndoes not divide by zero (`allowedStage` contains zero and the source label\ntype is nonempty), that positivity is proved first on finite matrix squares\nand then extended by closedness from the dense algebraic image, and that the\nregional positivity proof uses only the already constructed C-star\nequivalence.  It also checked that the old `ProductStateBound` occurs only in\nthe preserved partial §8 material and explanatory text, not as an argument of\nthe recovery declarations.  Compilation and axiom reports validate the Lean\nproof artifacts; they do not prove the inherited P53/P55D geometric premises\nor any later operator-algebraic classification.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the exact archive, its quarantine extraction, the\nintegrated P56R candidate, and this closeout review.  Existing modified\n`PLAN.md`, packet/decision files, earlier candidates, and earlier reviews were\npreserved.  No commit, push, manuscript edit, archive build, dependency update,\nor dependency fetch was performed.\n# P57A closeout review — vacuum-restricted infinite-tensor pre-Hilbert core\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated shared-infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n\nAristotle task `563e769a-0e9b-4395-9895-e03c81c26851` was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-205100d0-563e769a.tar.gz`\nand extracted, without a build, dependency update, or fetch, only under\n`aristotle_responses/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-205100d0-563e769a-quarantine/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean` was\nintegrated into the live project.  The raw archive and quarantine extraction\nremain intact response records.  No manuscript file was changed.\n\nThe quarantined response incorrectly said that the nominated local source\n`<original-home>/Projects/current/bound_beating/formalize_itp/Formalization/InfiniteTensorProductHilbert.lean`\nwas absent.  It is present.  Local comparison confirms that the integrated\nmodule independently re-expresses the source's proved finite-support core,\nbut with a finite-Gram-coordinate proof route rather than importing the other\nproject.  I corrected that provenance comment in the live integrated module;\nthis changes documentation only.  The candidate and quarantine SHA-256 values\ntherefore differ:\n\n- live: `c4936227e370cd0d04c32f4d62807003ed688afba9ca661a330c696a5c75feca`;\n- quarantined response: `ee8862347e606cc8ac629e3baa8909354ad288da9a4f5502c8639fa595633c52`.\n\n## Source, assumptions, and exact declarations\n\nThis is **infrastructure only**, not a manuscript-facing assertion.  The\ncandidate imports only `Mathlib`; it does not import the `bound_beating`\nproject or any other package result.\n\nAll generic results use only the packet-authorized assumptions\n`[DecidableEq ι]`, `[∀ i, NormedAddCommGroup (E i)]`, and\n`[∀ i, InnerProductSpace ℂ (E i)]`.  The normalization premise\n\n```lean\nhΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1\n```\n\nis used exactly where padding a product outside active support, positivity,\nfinite-mode kernel realization, finite-mode evaluation, and the exported\npre-inner-product core require it.  No completion, density, positivity, or\nexternal analytical premise was added.\n\nThe load-bearing live declarations are:\n\n- `exists_gram_coords` (lines 64--77), finite coordinates for every finite\n  Gram matrix;\n- `exists_finiteMode_realization` (88--104) and\n  `sum_prod_inner_nonneg` (109--122), realizing the product kernel as a\n  norm square in a finite coordinate tensor model;\n- `VacuumTensor` (128--134), `kern` (153--154), and\n  `kern_eq_prod_of_subset` (158--164), defining the finite-support\n  elementary tensors and support-independent kernel;\n- `itpInner` (183--184), `conj_itpInner_symm` (220--231),\n  `itpInner_add_left` (234--247), and `itpInner_smul_left` (250--262),\n  the algebraic sesquilinear extension;\n- `itpInner_nonneg` (266--285), positivity for an arbitrary finite linear\n  combination, and `re_itpInner_nonneg` (288--291);\n- `itpCore` (295--301), the exported\n  `PreInnerProductSpace.Core ℂ (ITPSpan Ω)`;\n- `vacuumVector` and `itpInner_vacuumVector` (309--322), whose\n  norm-square is one; and\n- `exists_finiteMode_realization_kern` (329--341) and\n  `itpInner_eq_finiteMode` (344--352), the finite-mode statements for the\n  actual vacuum-restricted kernel and algebraic span.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The finite-support elementary tensors, their finite-product kernel, the free finite span, sesquilinearity, finite-mode realization, positivity on arbitrary finite sums, the pre-inner-product core, and the algebraic vacuum norm-square-one theorem are all explicit proved declarations. |\n| partial | Quotienting the null space, completion, and an infinite tensor-product Hilbert-space instance are deliberately absent. |\n| blocked | None at P57A scope.  The local Mathlib snapshot lacks a ready-made inner-product API for a general `PiTensorProduct`; the candidate avoids that gap by proving the finite Gram-coordinate realization in `EuclideanSpace`, which suffices for the stated kernel positivity theorem. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at the stated scope.  The changed\nroute is the finite-Gram-coordinate proof of positivity, instead of importing\nor copying an optional completion wrapper from the source workspace.  It adds\nno premises and neither weakens the algebraic target nor supplies a\ncompletion.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P57A, Lane `shared` — correct.\n- **Predecessors:** none — correct.  The module is self-contained and imports\n  only Mathlib; it uses no package result that was merely remotely finished.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: it supplies a proved finite-support\n  vacuum-restricted algebraic ITP kernel and pre-inner-product core, so P57\n  need not recreate that algebraic layer.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The module has no quotient or\n  completion, no completed infinite tensor-product Hilbert space, no\n  pure/mixed GNS tensor splitting, no spatial von Neumann tensor product, no\n  factor classification, and no manuscript state identity.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct` —\n  passed in the already-built live project (8026 jobs).\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct Formalization`\n  — passed in the live project.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `#print axioms` for `exists_gram_coords`,\n  `exists_finiteMode_realization`, `sum_prod_inner_nonneg`,\n  `kern_eq_prod_of_subset`, `itpInner_nonneg`, `itpCore`,\n  `itpInner_vacuumVector`, and `exists_finiteMode_realization_kern` —\n  each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- A forbidden-declaration scan found no `sorry`, `admit`, user\n  `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or\n  `native_decide`; the only textual matches are explanatory prose.\n- Direct-import audit: exactly `import Mathlib`; no external-project import.\n  `git diff --check` for the integrated module passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The review checked that the normalization\npremise is used to justify only padding outside the finite active set, that\npositivity reduces the complete finite Finsupp support to an actual finite\ncoordinate norm square, and that the `PreInnerProductSpace.Core` receives\nthe real-part nonnegativity required by its interface.  It also checked the\nempty-active-set vacuum calculation separately, so its norm-square-one\nstatement is not being promoted to a general product-padding theorem without\n`hΩ`.  Builds and axiom reports validate the formal declarations, but do\nnot create the intentionally omitted quotient, completion, GNS, or spatial\noperator-algebra results.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P57A candidate, this closeout review, the\nexact raw archive, and its quarantine extraction.  The repository already had\nthe listed modified plan/task files and untracked earlier candidates/reviews;\nthey were not overwritten or otherwise changed.  No commit, push, archive\nbuild, dependency update, dependency fetch, or manuscript modification was\nperformed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
