{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' aristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57-sznchb36_aristotle/ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Summary of changes for run 36471af9-1931-4a1d-abb2-b06cdea11960\n## P57 — product GNS tensor factorization: complete\n\nAll work is in the single packet-authorized module `AristotleCandidates/ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` (~1070 lines). No other file was modified.\n\n**Lean compilation (verified separately from mathematical content).** `lake build AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensorFactorization` succeeds with zero errors and zero linter warnings. A scan of the file finds no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe` or `implemented_by`. `#print axioms` on all main declarations reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.\n\n**Setup and auxiliary assumptions.** Everything is developed for an explicit bundle `ProductGNSData`, whose fields list *every* premise used: two commuting unital `⋆`-homomorphisms `pureEmb`, `mixedEmb` into a total C⋆-algebra; positive functionals `pureState`, `mixedState`, `totalState`; `commuting`; `product` (`ω(ι₁a·ι₂b) = ω₁(a)ω₂(b)`); `state_norm_le` (contractivity of the total functional); and `span_dense` (norm density of the span of elementary products). Non-vacuity is certified by `trivialProductGNSData` on ℂ and the resulting `Nonempty` instance.\n\n**1. Checked infrastructure built here.** Completion-extension helpers (`clmExtend`, `extendOfBound`, `coeCLM`); the algebra of elementary products (`prodElt_mul`, `prodElt_star_mul`, `totalState_prodElt_inner`); the product map `prodCLM` with the exact inner-product factorization `inner_prodCLM`; the induced isometry `tensorLiftIsometry` of the algebraic tensor product `K_pure ⊗[ℂ] K_mixed` and its completion; dense range and surjectivity of the induced map; the elementary tensor operators `tensorMapₗ`/`tensorOp`/`tensorOpC` with the norm bound `norm_tensorMapₗ_le` derived from the intertwining identity.\n\n**2. Theorems recovered in the manuscript's intended form** (`main.tex:1945-1985`): `productGNSUnitary : TensorGNS ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] TotalGNS` (the split `H_ω̃ = K ⊗ K'`); the intertwining identity proved on the dense finite-word subspace (`prodCLM_intertwine_coe`) and then everywhere by continuity (`prodCLM_intertwine`, `tensorUnitaryCLM_tensorOpC`, `unitaryConj_tensorOpC`); the norm-density step `centralizer_representedProductSet`; `bicommutant_elementary_eq_spatial`; and the represented-algebra identification `unitaryConj_image_spatialTensorAlgebra`, i.e. conjugation by the product GNS unitary carries the spatial tensor product of the two represented factor algebras exactly onto `π(Total)''`.\n\n**3. Conditional statements.** None beyond the explicit `ProductGNSData` fields listed above.\n\n**4. Obstructions still open, documented in the module docstring.** Pinned Mathlib has no von Neumann spatial tensor product (no `VonNeumannAlgebra` tensor construction, no commutation theorem `(M ⊗̄ N)' = M' ⊗̄ N'`, no `(M ⊗ 1)' = M' ⊗̄ B(K)`); rather than assume any interface, the spatial tensor product is *defined* locally by its standard bicommutant formula `({π₁(a) ⊗ 1} ∪ {1 ⊗ π₂(b)})''` and the identification is proved for it — the missing part is the further theory of that object. Mathlib also lacks a general bound `‖T ⊗ S‖ ≤ ‖T‖‖S‖` on algebraic tensor products of inner-product spaces (only `TensorProduct.mapIsometry`), so boundedness is derived from the constructed intertwining; and it has no inner product on `PiTensorProduct`, so an infinite tensor product would have to be built by hand.\n\n**Plan alignment.** Lane H; predecessors P54, P56R, P57A and the checked GNS/bicommutant transport modules are imported and used only through their integrated results. No forbidden downstream claim is made: nothing asserts that either factor is a factor, no mixed-factor classification, no regional factorhood, and no trace/weight dichotomy; `B(K)` is never claimed to be the represented pure factor.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
