 product of the two represented factor algebras exactly onto `π(Total)''`.\naristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57-sznchb36_aristotle/ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md:16:**4. Obstructions still open, documented in the module docstring.** Pinned Mathlib has no von Neumann spatial tensor product (no `VonNeumannAlgebra` tensor construction, no commutation theorem `(M ⊗̄ N)' = M' ⊗̄ N'`, no `(M ⊗ 1)' = M' ⊗̄ B(K)`); rather than assume any interface, the spatial tensor product is *defined* locally by its standard bicommutant formula `({π₁(a) ⊗ 1} ∪ {1 ⊗ π₂(b)})''` and the identification is proved for it — the missing part is the further theory of that object. Mathlib also lacks a general bound `‖T ⊗ S‖ ≤ ‖T‖‖S‖` on algebraic tensor products of inner-product spaces (only `TensorProduct.mapIsometry`), so boundedness is derived from the constructed intertwining; and it has no inner product on `PiTensorProduct`, so an infinite tensor product would have to be built by hand.\naristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57-sznchb36_aristotle/ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md:18:**Plan alignment.** Lane H; predecessors P54, P56R, P57A and the checked GNS/bicommutant transport modules are imported and used only through their integrated results. No forbidden downstream claim is made: nothing asserts that either factor is a factor, no mixed-factor classification, no regional factorhood, and no trace/weight dichotomy; `B(K)` is never claimed to be the represented pure factor.\naristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57-sznchb36_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean:4:import AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct\naristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57-sznc