{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba aristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57-sznchb36_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean | sed -n '1,420p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\timport Mathlib\n     2\timport AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation\n     3\timport AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity\n     4\timport AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct\n     5\timport AristotleCandidates.GNSCommutantConjugation\n     6\timport AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore\n     7\timport AristotleCandidates.VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem\n     8\t\n     9\t/-!\n    10\t# P57 — product GNS tensor factorization\n    11\t\n    12\t**Context declaration.**  Source basis: `main.tex:1945-1985`.  Package `P57`, Lane `H`.\n    13\tPredecessors `P54` (`UHFReferenceRepresentation`), `P56R` (`RegionalProductStateIdentity`) and\n    14\t`P57A` (`VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct`), together with the checked GNS/bicommutant\n    15\ttransport modules `GNSCommutantConjugation`, `BicommutantVonNeumannCore` and\n    16\t`VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem`, are imported.\n    17\t\n    18\tThe manuscript step formalized here is the passage\n    19\t\n    20\t* `H_ω̃ = K ⊗ K'` (the GNS Hilbert space of a product state splits as a Hilbert tensor product of\n    21\t  the GNS spaces of the two factor states), and\n    22\t* `π_ω̃(P_I)'' = (represented pure factor) ⊗̄ (represented mixed factor)` (the represented regional\n    23\t  algebra is the spatial tensor product of the two represented factor algebras).\n    24\t\n    25\t## Data and auxiliary assumptions\n    26\t\n    27\tEverything is developed for the explicit bundle `ProductGNSData`, whose fields list *all*\n    28\tauxiliary premises used anywhere in this file:\n    29\t\n    30\t* two unital `⋆`-homomorphisms `pureEmb : Pure →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Total` and `mixedEmb : Mixed →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Total`\n    31\t  of C⋆-algebras;\n    32\t* positive linear functionals `pureState`, `mixedState`, `totalState`;\n    33\t* `commuting` — the two embedded factors commute elementwise;\n    34\t* `product` — `totalState (ι₁ a · ι₂ b) = pureState a · mixedState b`;\n    35\t* `state_norm_le` — `totalState` is norm-decreasing (automatic for a state on a unital\n    36\t  C⋆-algebra, but assumed here as an explicit premise rather than re-derived);\n    37\t* `span_dense` — the linear span of the elementary products `ι₁ a · ι₂ b` is norm dense in\n    38\t  `Total`.\n    39\t\n    40\tNo further hypothesis, interface, axiom, or completion assumption is introduced anywhere: there\n    41\tare **no** `axiom`, `sorry`, `opaque`, `unsafe` or `implemented_by` declarations in this file, and\n    42\tno supplied (unproved) spatial von Neumann closure facts.\n    43\t\n    44\t## Classification of the results\n    45\t\n    46\t**(1) Checked infrastructure constructed in this packet.**\n    47\t\n    48\t* `clmExtend`, `extendOfBound`, `coeCLM`, `norm_clmExtend_le` — extension of bounded maps to\n    49\t  completions (needed because `LinearMap.mkContinuous` does not elaborate directly out of\n    50\t  `PositiveLinearMap.PreGNS` into operator-valued codomains).\n    51\t* `prodElt`, `prodElt_mul`, `prodElt_star_mul`, `totalState_prodElt_inner`, `preInner_prodElt`,\n    52\t  `norm_prodElt` — the algebra of elementary product elements and the factorization of the GNS\n    53\t  inner product on them.\n    54\t* `prodCLM`, `inner_prodCLM` — the bilinear product map `K_pure × K_mixed → H_ω̃`, with the\n    55\t  exact inner-product factorization `⟪x ⊗ y, x' ⊗ y'⟫ = ⟪x, x'⟫ ⟪y, y'⟫`.\n    56\t* `tensorLiftₗ`, `norm_tensorLiftₗ`, `tensorLiftIsometry`, `tensorUnitaryCLM` — the induced\n    57\t  isometry of the algebraic tensor product `TensorPre = K_pure ⊗[ℂ] K_mixed` and of its\n    58\t  completion `TensorGNS`.\n    59\t* `totalCoe`, `denseRange_tensorUnitaryCLM`, `surjective_tensorUnitaryCLM`.\n    60\t* `tensorMapₗ`, `norm_tensorMapₗ_le`, `tensorOp`, `tensorOpC` — the elementary tensor operators\n    61\t  `π₁(a) ⊗ π₂(b)`; their boundedness is *derived* from the intertwining identity and the\n    62\t  isometry property, since pinned Mathlib has no general bound `‖T ⊗ S‖ ≤ ‖T‖ ‖S‖` on an\n    63\t  algebraic tensor product of inner-product spaces.\n    64\t\n    65\t**(2) Theorems recovered in the manuscript's intended form (for `ProductGNSData`).**\n    66\t\n    67\t* `productGNSUnitary : TensorGNS ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] TotalGNS` — the canonical GNS unitary\n    68\t  `K_pure ⊗ K_mixed ≅ H_ω̃`; this is the manuscript's `H_ω̃ = K ⊗ K'`.\n    69\t* `prodCLM_intertwine_coe` (intertwining on the dense subspace of classes of algebra elements,\n    70\t  i.e. on finite words) and `prodCLM_intertwine`, `tensorUnitaryCLM_tensorOpC` (intertwining\n    71\t  everywhere, by continuity).\n    72\t* `unitaryConj_tensorOpC` — conjugation by the unitary maps `π₁(a) ⊗ π₂(b)` to\n    73\t  `π_ω̃(ι₁ a · ι₂ b)`.\n    74\t* `centralizer_representedProductSet` — the elementary product operators and the whole\n    75\t  represented algebra have the same commutant.\n    76\t* `bicommutant_elementary_eq_spatial` — the bicommutant of the elementary tensor operators equals\n    77\t  `spatialTensorAlgebra`, the spatial von Neumann tensor product of the two represented factor\n    78\t  algebras, defined as usual as `({π₁(a) ⊗ 1} ∪ {1 ⊗ π₂(b)})''`.\n    79\t* `unitaryConj_image_spatialTensorAlgebra` — the manuscript's algebra identification:\n    80\t  `U (M_pure ⊗̄ M_mixed) U⋆ = π_ω̃(Total)''`.\n    81\t\n    82\t* `idPositive`, `trivialProductGNSData` and the resulting `Nonempty ProductGNSData` instance — a\n    83\t  non-vacuity witness showing that the fields of `ProductGNSData` are jointly satisfiable (the\n    84\t  witness is the trivial one on `ℂ`; it only certifies non-vacuity of the hypotheses).\n    85\t\n    86\t**(3) Conditional statements.**  None beyond the explicit fields of `ProductGNSData` listed\n    87\tabove; in particular the density premise `span_dense` and the contractivity premise\n    88\t`state_norm_le` are used and are stated as fields.\n    89\t\n    90\t**(4) Source / Mathlib obstructions still open.**\n    91\t\n    92\t* Pinned Mathlib has no von Neumann *spatial tensor product* `M ⊗̄ N` of two von Neumann algebras\n    93\t  acting on Hilbert spaces `H`, `K`: there is no `VonNeumannAlgebra` tensor construction, no\n    94\t  commutation theorem `(M ⊗̄ N)' = M' ⊗̄ N'`, and no `(M ⊗ 1)' = M' ⊗̄ B(K)`.  We therefore *define*\n    95\t  the spatial tensor product concretely as the bicommutant\n    96\t  `({π₁(a) ⊗ 1} ∪ {1 ⊗ π₂(b)})''` (`spatialTensorAlgebra`), which is the standard definition, and\n    97\t  prove the identification for it.  What is *not* available is the further theory of that object\n    98\t  (commutation theorem, slice maps, normal product extensions).\n    99\t* Pinned Mathlib has no bound `‖T ⊗ S‖ ≤ ‖T‖ ‖S‖` for general bounded `T`, `S` on the algebraic\n   100\t  tensor product of inner-product spaces (only `TensorProduct.mapIsometry` for isometries).  The\n   101\t  boundedness needed here is obtained instead from the constructed intertwining identity.\n   102\t* Pinned Mathlib has no inner product on `PiTensorProduct`, so an *infinite* tensor product of\n   103\t  Hilbert spaces has to be built by hand; that is why the split here is stated for a two-factor\n   104\t  product state, exactly as the manuscript's `K ⊗ K'`.\n   105\t\n   106\t**Forbidden downstream claims are not made.**  Nothing here asserts that either factor is a\n   107\tfactor, no mixed-factor classification, no regional factorhood, and no trace or weight dichotomy;\n   108\t`B(K)` is never claimed to be the represented pure factor (that would need irreducibility of the\n   109\tpure-state representation, which is not part of this packet).\n   110\t-/\n   111\t\n   112\tset_option maxHeartbeats 1000000\n   113\tset_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000\n   114\t\n   115\topen scoped InnerProductSpace ComplexOrder TensorProduct\n   116\topen UniformSpace\n   117\t\n   118\tnamespace AristotleCandidates\n   119\tnamespace ProductGNSTensor\n   120\t\n   121\tuniverse u\n   122\t\n   123\t/-! ## 0. Two pieces of completion infrastructure -/\n   124\t\n   125\tsection Completions\n   126\t\n   127\tvariable {X Y : Type*} [SeminormedAddCommGroup X] [NormedSpace ℂ X]\n   128\t    [NormedAddCommGroup Y] [NormedSpace ℂ Y] [CompleteSpace Y]\n   129\t\n   130\t/-- Extension of a continuous linear map to the completion of its domain, when the codomain is\n   131\talready complete. -/\n   132\tnoncomputable def clmExtend (f : X →L[ℂ] Y) : Completion X →L[ℂ] Y where\n   133\t  toFun := Completion.extension f\n   134\t  map_add' x y := by\n   135\t    induction x, y using Completion.induction_on₂ with\n   136\t    | hp =>\n   137\t      exact isClosed_eq (Completion.continuous_extension.comp continuous_add)\n   138\t        (Continuous.add (Completion.continuous_extension.comp continuous_fst)\n   139\t          (Completion.continuous_extension.comp continuous_snd))\n   140\t    | ih a b =>\n   141\t      rw [← Completion.coe_add, Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous,\n   142\t        Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous, Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous,\n   143\t        map_add]\n   144\t  map_smul' c x := by\n   145\t    induction x using Completion.induction_on with\n   146\t    | hp =>\n   147\t      exact isClosed_eq (Completion.continuous_extension.comp (continuous_const_smul c))\n   148\t        ((continuous_const_smul (c : ℂ)).comp Completion.continuous_extension)\n   149\t    | ih a =>\n   150\t      rw [← Completion.coe_smul, Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous,\n   151\t        Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous, RingHom.id_apply, f.map_smul]\n   152\t  cont := Completion.continuous_extension\n   153\t\n   154\t@[simp] theorem clmExtend_coe (f : X →L[ℂ] Y) (a : X) : clmExtend f (a : Completion X) = f a :=\n   155\t  Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous a\n   156\t\n   157\t/-- The canonical inclusion of a seminormed complex vector space into its completion, as a\n   158\tcontinuous linear map. -/\n   159\tnoncomputable def coeCLM (X : Type*) [SeminormedAddCommGroup X] [NormedSpace ℂ X] :\n   160\t    X →L[ℂ] Completion X where\n   161\t  toFun x := (x : Completion X)\n   162\t  map_add' x y := Completion.coe_add x y\n   163\t  map_smul' r x := Completion.coe_smul r x\n   164\t  cont := Completion.continuous_coe X\n   165\t\n   166\t@[simp] theorem coeCLM_apply (X : Type*) [SeminormedAddCommGroup X] [NormedSpace ℂ X] (x : X) :\n   167\t    coeCLM X x = (x : Completion X) := rfl\n   168\t\n   169\t/-- Extension to the completion of a bounded additive and `ℂ`-homogeneous map into a complete\n   170\tnormed space.  This packaging avoids elaborating an intermediate `LinearMap` whose instance\n   171\tpath differs from the seminormed one on GNS pre-Hilbert type synonyms. -/\n   172\tnoncomputable def extendOfBound (f : X → Y) (C : ℝ) (hadd : ∀ x y, f (x + y) = f x + f y)\n   173\t    (hsmul : ∀ (r : ℂ) (x : X), f (r • x) = r • f x) (hb : ∀ x, ‖f x‖ ≤ C * ‖x‖) :\n   174\t    Completion X →L[ℂ] Y :=\n   175\t  clmExtend (LinearMap.mkContinuous\n   176\t    { toFun := f, map_add' := hadd, map_smul' := hsmul } C hb)\n   177\t\n   178\t@[simp] theorem extendOfBound_coe (f : X → Y) (C : ℝ) (hadd : ∀ x y, f (x + y) = f x + f y)\n   179\t    (hsmul : ∀ (r : ℂ) (x : X), f (r • x) = r • f x) (hb : ∀ x, ‖f x‖ ≤ C * ‖x‖) (a : X) :\n   180\t    extendOfBound f C hadd hsmul hb (a : Completion X) = f a :=\n   181\t  clmExtend_coe _ _\n   182\t\n   183\ttheorem norm_clmExtend_le (f : X →L[ℂ] Y) (C : ℝ) (hC : ∀ a, ‖f a‖ ≤ C * ‖a‖) (x : Completion X) :\n   184\t    ‖clmExtend f x‖ ≤ C * ‖x‖ := by\n   185\t  induction x using Completion.induction_on with\n   186\t  | hp => exact isClosed_le (by fun_prop) (by fun_prop)\n   187\t  | ih a => rw [clmExtend_coe, Completion.norm_coe]; exact hC a\n   188\t\n   189\tend Completions\n   190\t\n   191\t/-! ## 1. Product-state data -/\n   192\t\n   193\t/-- The data of a product state: a total C⋆-algebra with two commuting unital C⋆-subalgebras\n   194\t(presented as unital ⋆-homomorphisms `pureEmb`, `mixedEmb`), and a positive functional on the\n   195\ttotal algebra which factorizes as a product of positive functionals on the two factors.\n   196\t\n   197\tAll auxiliary premises are explicit fields:\n   198\t\n   199\t* `commuting` — the two embedded algebras commute elementwise;\n   200\t* `product` — the state factorizes on products of the two factors;\n   201\t* `state_norm_le` — the total functional is norm-decreasing (true for any state on a unital\n   202\t  C⋆-algebra, assumed here rather than re-derived);\n   203\t* `span_dense` — the linear span of the product elements is norm dense in the total algebra.\n   204\t-/\n   205\tstructure ProductGNSData where\n   206\t  /-- The \"pure\" tensor factor algebra. -/\n   207\t  Pure : Type u\n   208\t  /-- The \"mixed\" tensor factor algebra. -/\n   209\t  Mixed : Type u\n   210\t  /-- The total algebra. -/\n   211\t  Total : Type u\n   212\t  [pureCStar : CStarAlgebra Pure]\n   213\t  [mixedCStar : CStarAlgebra Mixed]\n   214\t  [totalCStar : CStarAlgebra Total]\n   215\t  [pureOrder : PartialOrder Pure]\n   216\t  [mixedOrder : PartialOrder Mixed]\n   217\t  [totalOrder : PartialOrder Total]\n   218\t  [pureStarOrdered : StarOrderedRing Pure]\n   219\t  [mixedStarOrdered : StarOrderedRing Mixed]\n   220\t  [totalStarOrdered : StarOrderedRing Total]\n   221\t  /-- The embedding of the pure factor. -/\n   222\t  pureEmb : Pure →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Total\n   223\t  /-- The embedding of the mixed factor. -/\n   224\t  mixedEmb : Mixed →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Total\n   225\t  /-- The state of the pure factor. -/\n   226\t  pureState : Pure →ₚ[ℂ] ℂ\n   227\t  /-- The state of the mixed factor. -/\n   228\t  mixedState : Mixed →ₚ[ℂ] ℂ\n   229\t  /-- The total (product) state. -/\n   230\t  totalState : Total →ₚ[ℂ] ℂ\n   231\t  /-- The two embedded factors commute. -/\n   232\t  commuting : ∀ (a : Pure) (b : Mixed), pureEmb a * mixedEmb b = mixedEmb b * pureEmb a\n   233\t  /-- The total state is the product state. -/\n   234\t  product : ∀ (a : Pure) (b : Mixed),\n   235\t    totalState (pureEmb a * mixedEmb b) = pureState a * mixedState b\n   236\t  /-- The total state is norm-decreasing. -/\n   237\t  state_norm_le : ∀ x : Total, ‖totalState x‖ ≤ ‖x‖\n   238\t  /-- The product elements span a dense subspace of the total algebra. -/\n   239\t  span_dense :\n   240\t    Dense ((Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range fun p : Pure × Mixed => pureEmb p.1 * mixedEmb p.2) :\n   241\t      Submodule ℂ Total) : Set Total)\n   242\t\n   243\tattribute [instance] ProductGNSData.pureCStar ProductGNSData.mixedCStar ProductGNSData.totalCStar\n   244\t  ProductGNSData.pureOrder ProductGNSData.mixedOrder ProductGNSData.totalOrder\n   245\t  ProductGNSData.pureStarOrdered ProductGNSData.mixedStarOrdered\n   246\t  ProductGNSData.totalStarOrdered\n   247\t\n   248\tnamespace ProductGNSData\n   249\t\n   250\tvariable (D : ProductGNSData)\n   251\t\n   252\t/-! ### 1.1 Elementary product elements -/\n   253\t\n   254\t/-- The elementary product element `ι₁ a · ι₂ b` of the total algebra. -/\n   255\tdef prodElt (a : D.Pure) (b : D.Mixed) : D.Total := D.pureEmb a * D.mixedEmb b\n   256\t\n   257\ttheorem prodElt_star_mul (a c : D.Pure) (b d : D.Mixed) :\n   258\t    star (D.prodElt a b) * D.prodElt c d = D.prodElt (star a * c) (star b * d) := by\n   259\t  have h1 : star (D.prodElt a b) = D.mixedEmb (star b) * D.pureEmb (star a) := by\n   260\t    simp [prodElt, star_mul, map_star]\n   261\t  calc star (D.prodElt a b) * D.prodElt c d\n   262\t      = D.mixedEmb (star b) * (D.pureEmb (star a) * D.pureEmb c) * D.mixedEmb d := by\n   263\t        rw [h1, prodElt]; simp only [mul_assoc]\n   264\t    _ = D.mixedEmb (star b) * D.pureEmb (star a * c) * D.mixedEmb d := by rw [map_mul]\n   265\t    _ = D.pureEmb (star a * c) * D.mixedEmb (star b) * D.mixedEmb d := by\n   266\t        rw [(D.commuting (star a * c) (star b)).symm]\n   267\t    _ = D.prodElt (star a * c) (star b * d) := by\n   268\t        rw [prodElt, map_mul D.mixedEmb, ← mul_assoc]\n   269\t\n   270\ttheorem prodElt_mul (a c : D.Pure) (b d : D.Mixed) :\n   271\t    D.prodElt a b * D.prodElt c d = D.prodElt (a * c) (b * d) := by\n   272\t  calc D.prodElt a b * D.prodElt c d\n   273\t      = D.pureEmb a * (D.mixedEmb b * D.pureEmb c) * D.mixedEmb d := by\n   274\t        simp only [prodElt, mul_assoc]\n   275\t    _ = D.pureEmb a * (D.pureEmb c * D.mixedEmb b) * D.mixedEmb d := by\n   276\t        rw [← D.commuting c b]\n   277\t    _ = D.prodElt (a * c) (b * d) := by\n   278\t        simp only [prodElt, map_mul, mul_assoc]\n   279\t\n   280\t@[simp] theorem prodElt_one_one : D.prodElt 1 1 = 1 := by simp [prodElt]\n   281\t\n   282\ttheorem totalState_prodElt_inner (a c : D.Pure) (b d : D.Mixed) :\n   283\t    D.totalState (star (D.prodElt a b) * D.prodElt c d)\n   284\t      = D.pureState (star a * c) * D.mixedState (star b * d) := by\n   285\t  rw [prodElt_star_mul, prodElt, D.product]\n   286\t\n   287\t/-! ### 1.2 The three GNS spaces -/\n   288\t\n   289\t/-- The GNS Hilbert space of the pure factor state. -/\n   290\tabbrev PureGNS : Type _ := D.pureState.GNS\n   291\t\n   292\t/-- The GNS Hilbert space of the mixed factor state. -/\n   293\tabbrev MixedGNS : Type _ := D.mixedState.GNS\n   294\t\n   295\t/-- The GNS Hilbert space of the total product state. -/\n   296\tabbrev TotalGNS : Type _ := D.totalState.GNS\n   297\t\n   298\t/-- The GNS representation of the pure factor. -/\n   299\tnoncomputable def pureRep : D.Pure →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (D.PureGNS →L[ℂ] D.PureGNS) :=\n   300\t  D.pureState.gnsStarAlgHom\n   301\t\n   302\t/-- The GNS representation of the mixed factor. -/\n   303\tnoncomputable def mixedRep : D.Mixed →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (D.MixedGNS →L[ℂ] D.MixedGNS) :=\n   304\t  D.mixedState.gnsStarAlgHom\n   305\t\n   306\t/-- The GNS representation of the total algebra. -/\n   307\tnoncomputable def totalRep : D.Total →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (D.TotalGNS →L[ℂ] D.TotalGNS) :=\n   308\t  D.totalState.gnsStarAlgHom\n   309\t\n   310\t/-! ### 1.3 The pre-GNS inner-product identity -/\n   311\t\n   312\ttheorem preInner_prodElt (a c : D.Pure) (b d : D.Mixed) :\n   313\t    ⟪D.totalState.toPreGNS (D.prodElt a b), D.totalState.toPreGNS (D.prodElt c d)⟫_ℂ\n   314\t      = ⟪D.pureState.toPreGNS a, D.pureState.toPreGNS c⟫_ℂ *\n   315\t        ⟪D.mixedState.toPreGNS b, D.mixedState.toPreGNS d⟫_ℂ := by\n   316\t  rw [PositiveLinearMap.preGNS_inner_def, PositiveLinearMap.preGNS_inner_def,\n   317\t    PositiveLinearMap.preGNS_inner_def]\n   318\t  simp only [PositiveLinearMap.ofPreGNS_toPreGNS]\n   319\t  exact D.totalState_prodElt_inner a c b d\n   320\t\n   321\ttheorem norm_prodElt (a : D.Pure) (b : D.Mixed) :\n   322\t    ‖D.totalState.toPreGNS (D.prodElt a b)‖\n   323\t      = ‖D.pureState.toPreGNS a‖ * ‖D.mixedState.toPreGNS b‖ := by\n   324\t  have h := D.preInner_prodElt a a b b\n   325\t  rw [inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K, inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K, inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K] at h\n   326\t  have hc : ((‖D.totalState.toPreGNS (D.prodElt a b)‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ)\n   327\t      = (((‖D.pureState.toPreGNS a‖ * ‖D.mixedState.toPreGNS b‖) ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) := by\n   328\t    push_cast\n   329\t    rw [mul_pow]\n   330\t    exact h\n   331\t  have h' : (‖D.totalState.toPreGNS (D.prodElt a b)‖ : ℝ) ^ 2\n   332\t      = (‖D.pureState.toPreGNS a‖ * ‖D.mixedState.toPreGNS b‖) ^ 2 := by\n   333\t    exact_mod_cast hc\n   334\t  have h1 : (0 : ℝ) ≤ ‖D.totalState.toPreGNS (D.prodElt a b)‖ := norm_nonneg _\n   335\t  have h2 : (0 : ℝ) ≤ ‖D.pureState.toPreGNS a‖ * ‖D.mixedState.toPreGNS b‖ :=\n   336\t    mul_nonneg (norm_nonneg _) (norm_nonneg _)\n   337\t  nlinarith [h', h1, h2]\n   338\t\n   339\t/-! ## 2. The product bilinear map on the two factor GNS spaces -/\n   340\t\n   341\t/-- For a fixed pure-factor element, the pre-GNS level map `b ↦ ι₁ a · ι₂ b`. -/\n   342\tnoncomputable def preProdₗ (a : D.Pure) : D.mixedState.PreGNS →ₗ[ℂ] D.totalState.PreGNS where\n   343\t  toFun b := D.totalState.toPreGNS (D.prodElt a (D.mixedState.ofPreGNS b))\n   344\t  map_add' x y := by\n   345\t    simp [prodElt, PositiveLinearMap.toPreGNS, PositiveLinearMap.ofPreGNS, mul_add]\n   346\t  map_smul' r x := by\n   347\t    have h : D.mixedState.ofPreGNS (r • x) = r • D.mixedState.ofPreGNS x := map_smul _ _ _\n   348\t    have h2 : D.prodElt a (r • D.mixedState.ofPreGNS x)\n   349\t        = r • D.prodElt a (D.mixedState.ofPreGNS x) := by\n   350\t      simp [prodElt]\n   351\t    show D.totalState.toPreGNS (D.prodElt a (D.mixedState.ofPreGNS (r • x)))\n   352\t        = r • D.totalState.toPreGNS (D.prodElt a (D.mixedState.ofPreGNS x))\n   353\t    rw [h, h2, map_smul]\n   354\t\n   355\t@[simp] theorem preProdₗ_apply (a : D.Pure) (b : D.Mixed) :\n   356\t    D.preProdₗ a (D.mixedState.toPreGNS b) = D.totalState.toPreGNS (D.prodElt a b) := rfl\n   357\t\n   358\ttheorem preProdₗ_add_left (a a' : D.Pure) (b : D.mixedState.PreGNS) :\n   359\t    D.preProdₗ (a + a') b = D.preProdₗ a b + D.preProdₗ a' b := by\n   360\t  simp [preProdₗ, prodElt, PositiveLinearMap.toPreGNS, PositiveLinearMap.ofPreGNS, add_mul]\n   361\t\n   362\ttheorem preProdₗ_smul_left (r : ℂ) (a : D.Pure) (b : D.mixedState.PreGNS) :\n   363\t    D.preProdₗ (r • a) b = r • D.preProdₗ a b := by\n   364\t  simp [preProdₗ, prodElt, PositiveLinearMap.toPreGNS, PositiveLinearMap.ofPreGNS]\n   365\t\n   366\ttheorem norm_preProdₗ (a : D.Pure) (b : D.mixedState.PreGNS) :\n   367\t    ‖D.preProdₗ a b‖ = ‖D.pureState.toPreGNS a‖ * ‖b‖ :=\n   368\t  D.norm_prodElt a (D.mixedState.ofPreGNS b)\n   369\t\n   370\t/-- The same map, valued in the total GNS Hilbert space. -/\n   371\tnoncomputable def preProd (a : D.Pure) : D.mixedState.PreGNS →L[ℂ] D.TotalGNS :=\n   372\t  (coeCLM D.totalState.PreGNS).comp\n   373\t    ((D.preProdₗ a).mkContinuous ‖D.pureState.toPreGNS a‖ (fun b => le_of_eq (D.norm_preProdₗ a b)))\n   374\t\n   375\t@[simp] theorem preProd_apply (a : D.Pure) (b : D.mixedState.PreGNS) :\n   376\t    D.preProd a b = ((D.preProdₗ a b : D.totalState.PreGNS) : D.TotalGNS) := rfl\n   377\t\n   378\ttheorem norm_preProd_le (a : D.Pure) (b : D.mixedState.PreGNS) :\n   379\t    ‖D.preProd a b‖ ≤ ‖D.pureState.toPreGNS a‖ * ‖b‖ := by\n   380\t  rw [preProd_apply, Completion.norm_coe]\n   381\t  exact le_of_eq (D.norm_preProdₗ a b)\n   382\t\n   383\t/-- The product map with the second variable completed. -/\n   384\tnoncomputable def prodRight (a : D.Pure) : D.MixedGNS →L[ℂ] D.TotalGNS :=\n   385\t  clmExtend (D.preProd a)\n   386\t\n   387\t@[simp] theorem prodRight_coe (a : D.Pure) (b : D.mixedState.PreGNS) :\n   388\t    D.prodRight a (b : D.MixedGNS) = ((D.preProdₗ a b : D.totalState.PreGNS) : D.TotalGNS) :=\n   389\t  clmExtend_coe _ _\n   390\t\n   391\ttheorem norm_prodRight_apply_le (a : D.Pure) (y : D.MixedGNS) :\n   392\t    ‖D.prodRight a y‖ ≤ ‖D.pureState.toPreGNS a‖ * ‖y‖ :=\n   393\t  norm_clmExtend_le _ _ (D.norm_preProd_le a) y\n   394\t\n   395\ttheorem prodRight_add (a a' : D.Pure) : D.prodRight (a + a') = D.prodRight a + D.prodRight a' := by\n   396\t  ext y\n   397\t  induction y using Completion.induction_on with\n   398\t  | hp => exact isClosed_eq (by fun_prop) (by fun_prop)\n   399\t  | ih b =>\n   400\t    simp only [prodRight_coe, ContinuousLinearMap.add_apply]\n   401\t    rw [← Completion.coe_add, D.preProdₗ_add_left]\n   402\t\n   403\ttheorem prodRight_smul (r : ℂ) (a : D.Pure) : D.prodRight (r • a) = r • D.prodRight a := by\n   404\t  ext y\n   405\t  induction y using Completion.induction_on with\n   406\t  | hp => exact isClosed_eq (by fun_prop) (by fun_prop)\n   407\t  | ih b =>\n   408\t    simp only [prodRight_coe, ContinuousLinearMap.smul_apply]\n   409\t    rw [← Completion.coe_smul, D.preProdₗ_smul_left]\n   410\t\n   411\t/-- The product bilinear map, with both variables completed: `prodCLM D x y` is the GNS vector\n   412\tof the total product state corresponding to the pair `(x, y)` of factor GNS vectors. -/\n   413\tnoncomputable def prodCLM :=\n   414\t  extendOfBound (X := D.pureState.PreGNS) (Y := D.MixedGNS →L[ℂ] D.TotalGNS)\n   415\t    (fun a => D.prodRight (D.pureState.ofPreGNS a)) 1\n   416\t    (fun x y => by\n   417\t      have h : D.pureState.ofPreGNS (x + y)\n   418\t          = D.pureState.ofPreGNS x + D.pureState.ofPreGNS y := map_add _ _ _\n   419\t      show D.prodRight (D.pureState.ofPreGNS (x + y))\n   420\t          = D.prodRight (D.pureState.ofPreGNS x) + D.prodRight (D.pureState.ofPreGNS y)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
